@page "/verify/proximity"
@layout MainLayout
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using Sorcha.Reader.Components
@attribute [Authorize]

@*
    Doorstep verification, IN PERSON and OFFLINE (Feature 185).

    The sibling of /verify, which does the same job ONLINE over HAIP. This one needs no signal at all: the
    two devices talk directly over Bluetooth. Same feature, different circumstances — which is why it lives
    under /verify/ rather than as a rival surface.

    ONE app, both roles. The BLE plugin can be a peripheral (showing a credential) or a central (reading one),
    so two phones with the wallet installed can complete an entire in-person check between them. A separate
    reader app would have needed new App Store Connect and Play records before any of it could be tested.

    The reader itself lives in Sorcha.Reader (a component library), so splitting it into its own product later
    costs nothing and duplicates nothing.
*@

<PageTitle>Check in person · Sorcha Wallet</PageTitle>

<ReaderView />
